    { math: 'W = F · d · cos θ', note: 'Mechanical work is force times displacement along the force\'s direction. Only the component along the movement counts — pushing sideways does no work. The physiotherapist\'s intuition for "harder at this angle, easier at that one" is this cosine at work.' },
