    { math: 'THR = HR<sub>rest</sub> + % (HR<sub>max</sub> − HR<sub>rest</sub>)', note: 'The Karvonen formula sets training heart rate from heart-rate reserve, with HR<sub>max</sub> ≈ 220 − age (or the better Tanaka equation, 208 − 0.7 × age). Exercise prescription is physiology turned into a number the patient can watch on a pulse monitor.' },
